## 4. Additions after the first green runs
- tests/test_dump_ctx.c stage_edges_and_piece_order: boundaries of stages 4 and 5 (max_prec 0, -1,
  WORD_MAX; 2^64 - 1 and 2^64 as p and q), a count 2^64 + 1 that must not wrap, and the four order
  keys of qclass pieces. Written to kill mutants foreseen by reading the code (not red-green). First
  run: 1 failed check, my own text "pieces 1 0 0 0 0 l ..." lacked the archimedean count; fixed. Every
  expectation of the test was then checked against proto/text_grammar.py (script in the session);
  one differs: "adf1 Q char ffffffffffffffff 1 ..." is UNSUPPORTED in the reference because its
  search for the primitive character refuses moduli above 10^5 (proto lines 18-19, a limit of the
  reference). The C answer DOMAIN is kept and commented in the test.
- src/dump.c dp_sb_finish: a check n + 1 <= cap (flint_abort otherwise), so that a mutant that
  under-allocates the output string is caught without a sanitizer.
- valgrind: the struct snapshots of the tests (memcmp of the output against a copy) read the
  4 padding bytes of adf_fball_struct and adf_scaled_struct, uninitialised: "Conditional jump or move
  depends on uninitialised value(s)" in test_dump.c fball_status. The tests now memset the
  struct to 0 before init. The library was not at fault.

## 5. After mutation run 1 (lanes/m1-dump/mutate_run1.txt: 300 mutants, 224 killed, 26 survived,
##    50 not compiled; tests without sanitizers)
- Code changed so that survivors that could not change any result no longer exist as mutants:
  one scratch arb for the balls that are parsed and not kept (3 survivors); the one-context form
  passed as the binding count DP_ONE_CONTEXT instead of a flag, and a caller's count SIZE_MAX moved
  to SIZE_MAX - 1 by dp_count_of so that it stays a count (5 survivors); the walk state zeroed with
  memset (2 survivors); dp_sb_fmpz asks for exactly the bytes it writes (1 survivor).
- Tests added (tests/test_dump_ctx.c) for the survivors that were claims not checked: binding
  counts of every type including SIZE_MAX (binding_counts_of_every_type); the grammar over the
  whole text before any limit (a syntax fault after an over-limit count or precision, a trailing
  token after an over-limit context); a fault in the last token of a ball of rfun, idclass,
  char, ffun, sball, idele. Every new expected status was checked against proto/text_grammar.py.
  The new tests passed on the code as it stood (they target mutants, not missing code).
- Mutation run 2 uses the sanitizers (make SAN=1 in the --make command), so that a mutant that
  leaks or writes past a buffer (drop of flint_free in dp_desc_set, drop of dp_sb_room in
  dp_sb_lit) is judged by ASan/LSan.

## 6. After mutation run 2 (lanes/m1-dump/mutate_run2.txt: sanitizers on; 300 mutants, 232 killed,
##    12 survived, 56 not compiled)
- Two survivors were claims not checked (ffun: the D M limit applied in the wrong walk; the
  comparison 8 D M > tokens left). Tests added to stage_edges_and_piece_order: a syntax fault after
